SOAPBOX: Always a fun contest. My usual pet peeves are still around and always will be: A person running will take three or more stations before identifying. Two stations seems ideal, more than that will cause S&Pers to move on. Secondly, don't use cut numbers in a serial number. It's fine in a signal report as it's always 599 anyway. I wish there was a study that showed how much time is wasted by asking for the serial number again because the op couldn't handle the cut numbers, especially above 35 WPM. Thirdly, leading zeros in serial numbers should NEVER be used - it's just wasting time. End of rant. Looking forward to the WW CW, SS, etc.!
